Title        =The Andrew User Interface System - For the Programmer
Version      =63L0  6.3 Linux version 0
Desc1        =Latest version of AUIS (aka ATK) 6.3
Desc2        =AUIS is an integrated set of tools that allow you to create,
Desc3        =use, and mail multi-media documents and apps containing
Desc4        =formatted text and embedded objects.
Desc5        =This package is aimed at the SOURCE CODE DEVELOPER.
Author       =Andrew Consortium
AuthorEmail  =info-andrew-request@andrew.cmu.edu
Maintainer   =Terry Gliedt
MaintEmail   =tpg@mr.net 
Site1        =sunsite.unc.edu
Path1        =pub/Linux/X11/andrew
File1        =auis63L0-src.tgz
FileSize1    =0.7MB 
Required1    =YOU MUST HAVE INSTALLED AUIS63L0-WP.TGZ FIRST.
Required2    =/bin/csh  (e.g. ln -sf /bin/tcsh /bin/csh)
Required3    =X Window System
CopyPolicy1  =Use, copy, modify, and distribute this software and its
CopyPolicy2  =documentation for any purpose is granted without fee.
Keywords     =ATK, AUIS, source development, multi-media
Comment1     =Installation instructions as ROOT:
Comment2     =   cd /
Comment3     =   tar xzf [path]/auis63L?-src.tgz
Comment4     =   /usr/andrew/etc/complete-setup src
Comment5     =   Read /usr/andrew/README.src
RelFiles1    =Adds to directory tree /usr/andrew
